  "recipe": {
    "technique": "Tapestry is a type of weaving. Various designs of looms can be used, including upright or \"high-warp\" looms, where the tapestry is stretched vertically in front of the weaver, or horizontal \"low-warp\" looms, which were usual in large medieval and Renaissance workshops, but later mostly used for smaller pieces. The weaver always works on the back of the piece, and is normally following a full-size drawn or painted cartoon, or possibly another tapestry; depending on the set up, this reverses (is a mirror image of) the tapestry image."
